## Mission
The mission of the _IJMS_ is to advance the communication of medical and health sciences scholarship involving medical students and recently graduated physicians while promoting scientific rigor, research integrity, editorial development, and international collaboration.
The Journal seeks to:
*   provide a visible and accessible platform for scientifically sound medical and health sciences scholarship;  
*   promote responsible research conduct, transparent reporting, and recognized methodological and ethical standards;  
*   support emerging authors in developing experience with scholarly publishing;  
*   strengthen editorial and peer-review competencies through supervised training and mentorship;  
*   reduce financial barriers to publishing and accessing medical research;  
*   encourage collaboration across countries, institutions, disciplines, and levels of experience; and  
*   contribute to a more inclusive and internationally representative medical literature.
The educational mission of the _IJMS_ does not reduce its scientific standards. Manuscripts are evaluated according to their rigor, ethical compliance, transparency, reporting quality, relevance, clarity, and contribution to the literature.
